# PHASE 1 – BRAINSTORMING & IDEATION

## 1. Introduction

The Brainstorming and Ideation Phase is the first phase of the project development process. In this phase, the project idea is identified by discussing different problems, possible solutions, user needs, and available technologies.

The main purpose of this phase is to select a suitable project idea that is useful, practical, and possible to implement within the available time and resources.

---

## 2. Project Idea

### Project Title

Employee Data Import and Management System

### Project Idea

The proposed project focuses on importing employee information from a spreadsheet and managing the imported employee records in a structured system.

Employee information such as Employee ID, Employee Name, Department, Email, and Location can be maintained systematically. The project aims to reduce manual data entry and make employee information easier to manage.

---

## 3. Problem Identification

In many organizations, employee information may initially be maintained using spreadsheets or manually entered into systems.

Manual data handling can create several problems:

* Repeated data entry
* Incorrect information
* Missing employee details
* Difficulty in maintaining large amounts of data
* Time-consuming data entry
* Difficulty in updating records
* Difficulty in checking imported records
* Increased possibility of human errors
* Poor organization of employee information
* Difficulty in testing imported data

Therefore, a systematic employee data import and management process is required.

---

## 4. Brainstorming

Brainstorming was conducted to identify possible solutions for managing employee information.

The following ideas were considered:

1. Manual employee data entry system
2. Spreadsheet-based employee management
3. Employee database management system
4. Employee data import using Excel
5. Automated employee data import
6. Employee record validation system
7. Employee dashboard
8. Employee search and filtering system
9. Employee data reporting system
10. Employee data management using ServiceNow

After considering the above ideas, an employee data import and management system was selected.

---

## 5. Why This Project Idea Was Selected

The project idea was selected because employee information is commonly maintained in organizations and requires proper organization.

The proposed system provides an opportunity to understand:

* Data importing
* Spreadsheet handling
* Database tables
* Field mapping
* Data validation
* Record management
* Transforming imported data
* Testing
* Documentation
* System demonstration

The project is also suitable for learning and demonstrating practical data management concepts.

---

## 6. Existing Problem

The existing manual process may involve entering employee information one record at a time.

For example:

Employee ID → Employee Name → Department → Email → Location

When the number of employees increases, entering every record manually becomes time-consuming.

There is also a possibility of entering incorrect or incomplete information.

---

## 7. Proposed Solution

The proposed solution is to import employee information from a spreadsheet into the system.

The general process is:

Spreadsheet
↓
Import Data
↓
Import Set / Staging
↓
Field Mapping
↓
Data Transformation
↓
Employee Table
↓
Employee Records
↓
Testing and Verification

This approach helps organize employee information and reduces repetitive manual data entry.

---

## 8. Objectives of the Project

The main objectives of the project are:

1. To import employee information from a spreadsheet.
2. To organize employee data in a structured format.
3. To reduce manual data entry.
4. To understand the data import process.
5. To map spreadsheet fields with system fields.
6. To transform imported data into the required format.
7. To validate employee records.
8. To test the imported records.
9. To identify and correct errors.
10. To maintain employee information systematically.
11. To provide a simple and understandable data management process.
12. To demonstrate the complete project workflow.

---

## 9. Target Users

The possible users of the system are:

* System administrators
* HR department
* Organization employees
* Data management staff
* Project administrators

The system can help authorized users manage employee information efficiently.

---

## 10. Expected Input

The project expects employee information in spreadsheet format.

Example:

| Employee ID | Employee Name | Department | Email                                         | Location   |
| ----------- | ------------- | ---------- | --------------------------------------------- | ---------- |
| SB-0001     | Arun Kumar    | IT         | [arun@example.com](mailto:arun@example.com)   | Chennai    |
| SB-0002     | Priya Devi    | HR         | [priya@example.com](mailto:priya@example.com) | Coimbatore |

The spreadsheet acts as the source of employee information.

---

## 11. Expected Output

After successful processing, the employee information should be available as structured records in the target employee table.

The output should contain:

* Employee ID
* Employee Name
* Department
* Email
* Location

The imported records should be checked to ensure that the information is correctly transferred.

---

## 12. Key Features Identified

The following features were identified during brainstorming:

### 12.1 Spreadsheet Import

Employee information can be imported from an Excel spreadsheet.

### 12.2 Data Mapping

Source spreadsheet fields can be mapped to the corresponding target fields.

### 12.3 Data Transformation

Imported data can be processed and transformed before being stored.

### 12.4 Record Management

Employee records can be viewed and managed in the target table.

### 12.5 Data Validation

Imported records can be checked for correctness and completeness.

### 12.6 Testing

The system can be tested using sample employee records.

### 12.7 Reporting

Employee information can be displayed in an organized form for easier understanding.

